# Home: bring both arms to the program's start, through the twin (ADR-0071).
#
# `cite_bringup.program.home.bring_to_start`: initialize every physical arm,
# measure the start on every side, and only where a side is not there move
# both arms there with one signal; then measure again. Nothing is retried. On a
# pair with a physical side the console first reads the twin's mode as SIM and
# asks the operator to clear the cell (ConfirmPart), and puts the twin back in
# SIM afterwards. Rejected unless Start robot has succeeded and the console is
# READY. Cancelling the goal is the same software stop as StopCell.
#
# Served under `/cite/<zone>/console/<NAME>` (ConsoleState.msg).

string NAME="home"

float64 speed_scale     # (0, 1] of the program's own speed, sent explicitly by
                        # the operator's panel. Never defaulted: a goal with 0, or
                        # any value outside (0, 1], is rejected (ADR-0071 decision 2)
---
bool success
string detail           # what was done, or which step failed and why
---
string step             # the step being done now, as the operator reads it
